om the\n    17\trepository (`list-labels`, paginated), so `local/labels.yml` is retired and a\n    18\tlabel absent from GitHub is reported, never invented. Briefs (the design record\n    19\tper issue) live in `local/briefs/`: agent input, not lifecycle state.\n    20\t\n    21\tEvery GitHub call goes through `local/bin/gh_common.py` — a module for Python\n    22\tcallers, and for the shell scripts a CLI (`pr-view`, `post-status`,\n    23\t`latest-statuses`, `ensure-pr-comment`, `post-review`, `merge-pr`,\n    24\t`issue-create`, `issue-close`, `snapshot`, …; `--help` lists them) owning CLI\n    25\tdiscovery, repository resolution, API version headers, bounded retry of\n    26\ttransient failures and the exit-2-with-stderr convention. Nothing else shells\n    27\tout to `gh`. `issue_new.py`, `issue_close.py`, `pr_open.py`, `ci.sh`,\n    28\t`review.sh`, `autofix.sh`, `pr_merge.py`, `github-sync.sh` take GitHub numbers;\n    29\t`track.py`, `validate_tree.py` and `export_issues.py` are deleted.\n    30\t\n    31\t* Branches: `issue-<github-number>-<slug>`, or `codex/issue-<number>-<slug>`\n    32\t  from an agent; `pr_open.py` rejects what `git check-ref-format` would.\n    33\t* Titles, slugs and branch names are **bracket-free**: bot-generated branch\n    34\t  names inherit those characters and \"`]` breaks part of the PR automation\n    35\t  stack\" (docs/CONTRIBUTING.md:122-124). A `:` in a *title* is fine\n    36\t  (`Tracking: …`), but not in a branch.\n    37\t* `autofix.sh`'s automated fix commits keep the exact subject prefixes\n    38\t  `[codex-auto-fix]` and `[codex-review-fix]`; its iteration counter and the\n    39\t  review skip key on them.  Operator and worker repairs use plain\n    40\t  `fix(review): …` / `fix(ci): …` subjects so the reviewer sees them.\n    41\t* `Closes #N` / `Fixes #N` auto-closes the issue on merge, `Addresses #N` does\n    42\t  not (docs/CONTRIBUTING.md:61-62) — and the numbers being GitHub's, that\n    43\t  footer is now literally what GitHub itself reads.\n    44\t\n    45\t## 2. Evidence contracts\n    46\t\n    47\tAll evidence binds to the **exact head SHA** (DESIGN.md invariant 2).\n    48\t\n    49\t**Commit statuses.** Ten canonical contexts, posted by `post-status`: one\n    50\t`local-ci/<step>` per CI step (`build`, `blueprint-render`, `paper-gaps`,\n    51\t`blueprint-sync`, `file-length`, `proof-debt`, `proof-evasion`,\n    52\t`statement-origin`), plus `local-ci/summary` and `local-review/summary`.\n    53\t`ci.sh` posts `pending` before each gate step and `success | failure | error`\n    54\tafter it; a gated-out step is a `success` saying it was skipped. The gate reads\n    55\tthe *latest* status per context (`latest-statuses`), never GitHub's combined\n    56\tstatus, silent as that is about contexts never posted. The run manifest is one\n    57\tPR comment marked `<!-- mipstarre-ci-manifest pr=N -->`, kept current by\n    58\t`ensure-pr-comment`: evidence for humans, while the statuses are the gate.\n    59\t\n    60\t**Review verdict.** One `COMMENT` review per head SHA, bound to `commit_id`,\n    61\tcarrying `<!-- mipstarre-review pr=N head=SHA -->`, the findings ledger, and the\n    62\tline `VERDICT: APPROVED | COMMENTED | CHANGES_REQUESTED (code=…, prose=…)`.\n    63\tUnchecked findings are ledger lines matching `^\\s*[-*]\\s*\\[ \\]`; clean means\n    64\t`APPROVED`, or `COMMENTED` with none of them. Adverse verdicts post as `COMMENT`\n    65\ttoo — a **single account** cannot approve its own pull request, so the review\n    66\tevent carries no authority — and adverseness travels in `local-review/summary`\n    67\t(`failure` for unresolved findings), which is the gate's review evidence.\n    68\t\n    69\t**Adjudication** (review.md §12) is a PR comment whose body starts with\n    70\t`ADJUDICATION` and contains `head=<SHA>` for the current head, one disposition\n    71\tline per remaining finding; `--adjudicated` takes nothing else.\n    72\t\n    73\t**Idempotency.** Every publishing step is **at most one mutation**: a paginated\n    74\tread finds the stable marker first and adopts that record instead of duplicating\n    75\tit (`commentOnce`, issue-automation.yml:403-417, now guarding retries rather than\n    76\twebhook redelivery); an ambiguous write stays pending for adoption.\n    77\t\n    78\t## 3. The merge gate\n    79\t\n    80\t`pr_merge.py <number>` is the only path to `main`: never `git merge` to main,\n    81\tnever push `main`. The merge is a REST `PUT …/pulls/{n}/merge` with the exact\n    82\t`sha` guard, issued by `gh_common.merge_pr` and verified against the merge\n    83\tcommit's topology (two parents, the frozen head second), behind seven gates\n    84\tthat refuse by default:\n    85\t\n    86\t1. the PR is open, unmerged and not a draft (`draft is False`, not merely\n    87\t   falsy), and reports a head SHA, a head ref and a base ref;\n    88\t2. the primary worktree is clean and on the base, and the local branch tip\n    89\t   equals the GitHub head SHA — the merge must be of the bytes built here;\n    90\t3. all eight `local-ci/<step>` contexts plus `local-ci/summary` are `success` on\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
