ument fixes a strategy $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\strategy^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{orac}}$ for the oracularized game\\\\\\\\n   159\\\\\\\\t``with value $1-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps$'' and applies the lemma to assume without loss of\\\\\\\\n   160\\\\\\\\tgenerality that it is projective.%\\\\\\\\n   161\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\footnote{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\path{references/qpbt-paper/10_oracularization.tex},\\\\\\\\n   162\\\\\\\\tlines~317--321.}\\\\\\\\n   163\\\\\\\\tHere the input is a given strategy, not the value of the game; the\\\\\\\\n   164\\\\\\\\tgiven-strategy form applies verbatim and preserves the value exactly, so the\\\\\\\\n   165\\\\\\\\tuse is justified by what the proof establishes.\\\\\\\\n   166\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   167\\\\\\\\tSecond, in the soundness proof for answer reduction, the argument assumes the\\\\\\\\n   168\\\\\\\\tstrict inequality $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\game) > 1-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps$ and concludes that there is a\\\\\\\\n   169\\\\\\\\tsymmetric projective strategy of value greater than $1-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps$.%\\\\\\\\n   170\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\footnote{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\path{references/qpbt-paper/11_answer_reduction.tex},\\\\\\\\n   171\\\\\\\\tlines~2322--2332.}\\\\\\\\n   172\\\\\\\\tWriting $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\game) = 1-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps_0$ with $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps_0 < \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps$ and applying the\\\\\\\\n   173\\\\\\\\tapproximate form with $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps' = (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps+\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps_0)/2$ produces a symmetric\\\\\\\\n   174\\\\\\\\tprojective strategy of value at least $1-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps' > 1-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps$.  A strict lower\\\\\\\\n   175\\\\\\\\tbound on the supremum thus passes through the approximate form; attainment is\\\\\\\\n   176\\\\\\\\tnot used.\\\\\\\\n   177\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   178\\\\\\\\tIn this project, the soundness statements of the Pauli basis test track\\\\\\\\n   179\\\\\\\\tquantify over strategies assumed to succeed with probability at least\\