e given-strategy\\\\\\\\n   204\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanid{exists\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_symmetric\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_projective\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_strategy\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_of\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_strategy}, linked to the\\\\\\\\n   205\\\\\\\\tsupport node, has the same hypothesis, exact value equality, and projective\\\\\\\\n   206\\\\\\\\tsymmetric conclusion as that node, and its proof is complete.\\\\\\\\n   207\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   208\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\section{Conclusion}\\\\\\\\n   209\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   210\\\\\\\\tThe verdict is a proof-level gap in the cited lemma: the symmetrization\\\\\\\\n   211\\\\\\\\targument proves the given-strategy and approximate forms, while the printed\\\\\\\\n   212\\\\\\\\tconclusion additionally asserts that the supremum defining $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\val^*(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\game)$ is\\\\\\\\n   213\\\\\\\\tattained, which does not follow.  The gap is harmless for the results built\\\\\\\\n   214\\\\\\\\ton the lemma, since both uses in the source, and all planned uses in this\\\\\\\\n   215\\\\\\\\tproject, proceed from a given strategy of value at least $1-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps$ or from a\\\\\\\\n   216\\\\\\\\tstrict lower bound on the value, for which the value-preserving construction\\\\\\\\n   217\\\\\\\\tsuffices.  Stage~4 has carried out the recommendation of this note: the\\\\\\\\n   218\\\\\\\\tgiven-strategy symmetrization lemma is formalized and proved as the workhorse\\\\\\\\n   219\\\\\\\\tstatement, while the source-labelled lemma keeps its source shape with the\\\\\\\\n   220\\\\\\\\tattainment step an explicit, tracked proof obligation.  If a later\\\\\\\\n   221\\\\\\\\tinvestigation settles the counterexample question for symmetric games, the\\\\\\\\n   222\\\\\\\\tstatement should then be reclassified from an unproved step to a documented\\\\\\\\n   223\\\\\\\\tstatement correction.\\\\\\\\n   224\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   225\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bibliographystyle{alpha}\\\\\\\\n   226\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bibliography{references}\\\\\\\\n   227\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   228\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\end{document}\\\\\\\\n     1\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\documentclass[11pt]{article}\\\\\\\\n     2\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n     3\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb}\\\\\\\\n     4\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\usepackage{xurl}\\\\\\\\n     5\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\usepackage[hidelinks]{hyperref}\\\\\\\\n     6\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\setlength{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\emergencystretch}{2em}\\\\\\\\n     7\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n     8\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\input{command}\\\\\\\\n     9\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    10\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\newcommand{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ind}{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\operatorname{ind}}\\\\\\\\n    11\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\renewcommand{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ghissue}[1]{%\\\\\\\\n    12\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\href{https://github.com/Dengnifer/MIPStarRE-A/issues/#1}{GitHub issue \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\##1}}\\\\\\\\n    13\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    14\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\title{Corrections to the Pauli-Test Winning Implications}\\\\\\\\n    15\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\author{}\\\\\\\\n    16\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\date{2026-09-04}\\\\\\\\n    17\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    18\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\begin{document}\\\\\\\\n    19\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\maketitle\\\\\\\\n    20\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    21\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\section{At a glance}\\\\\\\\n    22\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    23\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\begin{itemize}\\\\\\\\n    24\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\textbf{Difficulty.} Low to medium.  The subtest implications are\\\\\\\\n    25\\\\\\\\t  direct after conditioning, but the printed proof uses an invalid parameter\\\\\\\\n    26\\\\\\\\t  reduction and two displayed formulas contain wrong indices.\\\\\\\\n    27\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\textbf{Estimated weight.} The formal work is the family of exact and\\\\\\\\n    28\\\\\\\\t  approximate winning implications, roughly 300--500 lines after the sampling\\\\\\\\n    29\\\\\\\\t  probability results are available.\\\\\\\\n    30\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\textbf{Mathlib/project split.} About 20\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\% finite-probability\\\\\\\\n    31\\\\\\\\t  bookkeeping and 80\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\% project-local game predicates, post-processing, and\\\\\\\\n    32\\\\\\\\t  state-dependent distance transfer.\\\\\\\\n    33\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\item \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\textbf{Key mathematical inputs.} Constant lower bounds for the\\\\\\\\n    34\\\\\\\\t  commuting and anticommuting events, data processing, and the one-way Magic\\\\\\\\n    35\\\\\\\\t  Square rigidity theorem.  The proof packets are \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ghissue{112} and\\\\\\\\n    36\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ghissue{113}.\\\\\\\\n    37\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\end{itemize}\\\\\\\\n    38\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    39\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\section{Key theorem forms}\\\\\\\\n    40\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    41\\\\\\\\tFor an admissible tuple $(q,m,d)$ and a strategy that wins the Pauli basis test\\\\\\\\n    42\\\\\\\\twith probability at least $1-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps$, each subtest has conditional failure\\\\\\\\n    43\\\\\\\\t$O(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps)$.  In particular, the Magic Square average is conditioned on\\\\\\\\n    44\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[\\\\\\\\n    45\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\gamma(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\omega)\\\\\\\\n    46\\\\\\\\t  =\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\tr\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\big((r_X\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ind_m(u_X))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\cdot(r_Z\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ind_m(u_Z))\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\big)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ne0,\\\\\\\\n    47\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\]\\\\\\\\n    48\\\\\\\\tand the low-degree line-evaluation family is completed on zero-direction lines\\\\\\\\n    49\\\\\\\\tby an additional outcome.  The observable consequence is\\\\\\\\n    50\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[\\\\\\\\n    51\\\\\\\\t  X^{r_X}(u_X)Z^{r_Z}(u_Z)\\\\\\\\n    52\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\approx_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\sqrt\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps}\\\\\\\\n    53\\\\\\\\t  (-1)^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\gamma(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\omega)}Z^{r_Z}(u_Z)X^{r_X}(u_X)\\\\\\\\n    54\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\]\\\\\\\\n    55\\\\\\\\ton average over all tuples.  These statements hold for every admissible\\\\\\\\n    56\\\\\\\\tparameter tuple; no assumption $6md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leq q$ is needed.\\\\\\\\n    57\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    58\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\section{The source assertions and discrepancies}\\\\\\\\n    59\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    60\\\\\\\\tThe source states the measurement implications at lines~197--265 and the\\\\\\\\n    61\\\\\\\\tobservable implications at lines~267--362 of the Pauli analysis\\\\\\\\n    62\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\cite[lines~197--362]{Ji2020MIPStar}.%\\\\\\\\n    63\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\footnote{See\\\\\\\\n    64\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\path{references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex}.}\\\\\\\\n    65\\\\\\\\tFour corrections are required.\\\\\\\\n    66\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    67\\\\\\\\tFirst, the displayed conditioning event for the Magic Square average omits\\\\\\\\n    68\\\\\\\\t$\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ind_m$ and writes the scalar expression\\\\\\\\n    69\\\\\\\\t$\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\tr((r_Xu_X)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\cdot(r_Zu_Z))$, even though $u_X,u_Z\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\in\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_q^m$ and the phase\\\\\\\\n    70\\\\\\\\tused by the game is defined through vectors in $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_q^{2^m}$.\\\\\\\\n    71\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    72\\\\\\\\tSecond, the proof assumes $6md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leq q$ and disposes of the complementary range\\\\\\\\n    73\\\\\\\\tby appealing to the final Pauli soundness theorem, whose proof uses the lemma\\\\\\\\n    74\\\\\\\\tunder discussion.  That appeal cannot prove the lemma as an unrestricted\\\\\\\\n    75\\\\\\\\tstandalone result.  The corrected exact probability calculation gives\\\\\\\\n    76\\\\\\\\tuniversal lower bounds for both conditioning events whenever the parameters\\\\\\\\n    77\\\\\\\\tare admissible, and removes this circular reduction.%\\\\\\\\n    78\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\footnote{The probability correction is documented separately in\\\\\\\\n    79\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\path{docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_anticommuting-probability.tex}.}\\\\\\\\n    80\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    81\\\\\\\\tThird, the source treats evaluation classes of a line measurement as a POVM\\\\\\\\n    82\\\\\\\\tindexed by $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_q$.  A zero-direction line admits nonconstant polynomial\\\\\\\\n    83\\\\\\\\trepresentatives with no well-defined value on its singleton image, so these\\\\\\\\n    84\\\\\\\\tclasses form only a sub-measurement.  Adding an outcome $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bot$ for the missing\\\\\\\\n    85\\\\\\\\tmass makes the consistency relation well typed; the point family is completed\\\\\\\\n    86\\\\\\\\tby a zero effect at the same outcome.\\\\\\\\n    87\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    88\\\\\\\\tFinally, the observable proof writes\\\\\\\\n    89\\\\\\\\t$Z^{r_X}(u_X)X^{r_Z}(u_Z)$ where the intended reversed product is\\\\\\\\n    90\\\\\\\\t$Z^{r_Z}(u_Z)X^{r_X}(u_X)$.  The source label prefix\\\\\\\\n    91\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\path{len:qld-win-implications-obs} is likewise a typographical error for\\\\\\\\n    92\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\path{lem:qld-win-implications-obs}.\\\\\\\\n    93\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    94\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\section{The corrected argument}\\\\\\\\n    95\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    96\\\\\\\\tEvery question type and every relevant subtest has a universal positive\\\\\\\\n    97\\\\\\\\tsampling weight.  For admissible parameters, $1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leq m\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leq q$, and the exact\\\\\\\\n    98\\\\\\\\tcalculation of the anticommuting probability gives probability at least\\\\\\\\n    99\\\\\\\\t$2^{-4}$ for the anticommuting event and at least $1/2$ for its complement.\\\\\\\\n   100\\\\\\\\tConditioning therefore enlarges rejection probabilities only by a universal\\\\\\\\n   101\\\\\\\\tfactor.  The measurement implications follow directly from their rejection\\\\\\\\n   102\\\\\\\\tevents, including the completed zero-direction outcome.  Data processing and\\\\\\\\n   103\\\\\\\\tthe agreement identities yield the observable relations; the corrected Magic\\\\\\\\n   104\\\\\\\\tSquare phase and reversed product then give the displayed signed commutation\\\\\\\\n   105\\\\\\\\tlaw.\\\\\\\\n   106\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   107\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\section{Blueprint and formalization status}\\\\\\\\n   108\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   109\\\\\\\\tThe blueprint uses the full phase $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\gamma$, completes the line-evaluation\\\\\\\\n   110\\\\\\\\tfamilies, proves the conditioning step with the universal probability bounds,\\\\\\\\n   111\\\\\\\\tand corrects the reversed product and label.  Its proof and correction remark\\\\\\\\n   112\\\\\\\\tcite this note.  The linked formal declarations use the same conditional\\\\\\\\n   113\\\\\\\\tdistributions and completed line outcomes, so their statements agree with the\\\\\\\\n   114\\\\\\\\tcorrected blueprint.  Their proofs remain open in the current tree.%\\\\\\\\n   115\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\footnote{The relevant declarations are \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanid{win\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_cons},\\\\\\\\n   116\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanid{win\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_low\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_degree}, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanid{win\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_pauli\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_basis\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_cons},\\\\\\\\n   117\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanid{win\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_comm}, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanid{win\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_comm\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_cons},\\\\\\\\n   118\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanid{win\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_magic\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_square}, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanid{win\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_ms\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_cons}, and their\\\\\\\\n   119\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\path{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\_approx} companions in\\\\\\\\n   120\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\doclink{MIPStarRE/QPBT/Observables/WinImplications.lean}.}\\\\\\\\n   121\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   122\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\section{Conclusion}\\\\\\\\n   123\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   124\\\\\\\\tThe winning implications remain valid for all admissible parameters, but the\\\\\\\\n   125\\\\\\\\tprinted proof does not establish that scope and several formulas need local\\\\\\\\n   126\\\\\\\\tcorrection.  Exact conditioning probabilities, the explicit missing outcome,\\\\\\\\n   127\\\\\\\\tand the corrected phase and operator indices give the form used by the Pauli\\\\\\\\n   128\\\\\\\\tbasis analysis.\\\\\\\\n   129\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   130\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bibliographystyle{alpha}\\\\\\\\n   131\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bibliography{references}\\\\\\\\n   132\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   133\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\end{document}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\nresults/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr184-20260905-04.jsonl-368-{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_188\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rg -n \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b(consum(e|es|ed|er|ers|ing)|provider(-side)?|downstream|upstream|formalized|formalization mark|linked declaration|Lean declaration|proof-level mark|statement-level mark|support node|workhorse)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\b\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" blueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\nresults/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr184-20260905-04.jsonl:369:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_188\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rg -n \\\