tement: the linked declaration differs from it in three further\\\\\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:137:\\\\\\\\tThe proof of Lemma~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{lem:symmetric-strat} yields, for each $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps' > \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps$, a symmetric projective strategy of value at least $1-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps'$. The conclusion as stated, at $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps' = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps$, does not follow from this: the dilated dimension $d$ may grow as $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps' \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\downarrow \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps$, and the supremum defining $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\operatorname{val}^*(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathfrak G)$ in Definition~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{def:tensor-product-value} need not be attained by any strategy. The symmetrization construction itself is value-preserving, so the conclusion does hold whenever the hypothesis supplies an actual strategy of value at least $1-\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps$ rather than only the value of the game; every use of the lemma in the source proceeds from such a strategy, or from a strict lower bound on the value, and therefore consumes only what the proof establishes. The gap and the available repairs are documented in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\cite{gap:qpbt_symmetrization-attainment}.\\\\\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:279:\\\\\\\\t% Status: the statement is final; no Lean declaration exists yet for the full disjunctive form, so this node carries no formalization marker.\\\\\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:1359:\\\\\\\\tLet $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathcal T$ be a set (the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\emph{type set}) and let $V$ be $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F^n$ for some integer $n \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ge 0$. A \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\emph{$\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathcal T$-typed family of $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ell$-level conditionally linear functions} (implicitly, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\emph{on $V$}) is a collection $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\{L_t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\}_{t \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathcal T}$ such that, for each $t \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathcal T$, $L_t$ is an $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ell$-level conditionally linear function on $V$. Finiteness of $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathcal T$ plays no part in this definition, which is therefore stated, as in the linked declaration, for an arbitrary type set; it is required from Definition~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{def:graph-distribution} onwards, where $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathcal T$ indexes a distribution. The source states the definition for a finite type set, and every type set occurring below is finite.\\\\\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:1394:% The Lean declaration typedCLDistribution is stated for arbitrary T-indexed families of maps\\\\\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:6:This chapter defines the two testing primitives underlying the question-reduction step: the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\emph{classical low individual degree game}, in its simultaneous form, and the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\emph{Pauli basis test}, a nonlocal game built from the classical game together with the Magic Square game. We state the quantum soundness of the classical game (Theorem~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{lem:ld-soundness}, imported, with the facts required by the identification, which remain to be proved, recorded in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\cite{gap:qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility}; see Remark~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{rem:ld-soundness-provider}), the rigidity of the Magic Square game (Theorem~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{thm:ms-rigidity}, imported), completeness of the Pauli basis test (Lemma~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{lem:pauli-completeness}), and the main soundness theorem for the Pauli basis test (Theorem~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{thm:pauli}), whose proof occupies Chapters~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{chap:qpbt-observables}--\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{chap:qpbt-extraction} and is completed in Chapter~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{chap:qpbt-extraction} only modulo the proof obligation documented in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\cite{gap:qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility}. The chapter closes with the qubit form of the soundness statement (Corollary~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{cor:pauli-binary}) and the canonical parameter choice with its soundness bound (Definition~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{def:introparams}, Lemma~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{lem:delta-bound}).\\\\\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:87:\\\\\\\\t% No completion mark: the linked declaration proves the distribution identity only, not the typed-family assertion. See the last paragraph of the statement; the open family assertion is tracked by issue 180.\\\\\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:89:\\\\\\\\tFix $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathsf{ldparams} = (q,m,d,k)$ as in Definition~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{def:ld-game}, let $L = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\{L_t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\}_{t \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathcal T^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}}$ be the family of Definition~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{def:ld-question-distribution}, and let $G^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}$ be the graph on $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathcal T^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}$ all of whose unordered pairs, self-loops included, are edges. Then the question distribution of $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathfrak{G}^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}$ is the $(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathcal T^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}, G^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}})$-typed conditionally linear distribution $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mu^{G^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}}_{L,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\,L}$ of Definition~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{def:typed-cl-distributions}. The linked declaration proves the distribution identity: the question distribution of $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathfrak{G}^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}$ equals the distribution that the construction of Definition~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{def:typed-cl-distributions} produces from the pair $(L, L)$ and the graph $G^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}$, a construction that is available for an arbitrary family of maps. It does not prove that $L$ is a $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathcal T^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{ld}}$-typed family of conditionally linear functions of one common level, which is what makes the right-hand side a typed conditionally linear distribution in the sense of Definition~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{def:typed-cl-distributions}: Lemmas~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{lem:ld-aline-level} and~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{lem:ld-dline-level} give the levels of $L_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathsf{ALine}}$ and $L_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathsf{DLine}}$, while the level of $L_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathsf{Point}}$ and the passage of the three maps to a common level are not formalized. That family assertion is open and is tracked as issue~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\#180, so the statement and the proof below carry no completion mark.\\\\\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:232:\\\\\\\\tQuantum soundness of the low individual degree test itself is the result of~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\cite{Ji2020LowIndividualDegree}; Remark~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{rem:ld-soundness-provider} relates the present statement to Theorem~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{thm:main-formal}, which proves that result.\\\\\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:235:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\begin{remark}[Relation to the low individual degree test of Chapter~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{chap:test}]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\label{rem:ld-soundness-provider}\\\\\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:397:\\\\\\\\tFix an admissible tuple $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathsf{qldparams} = (q,m,d)$ (Definition~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{def:admissible}) and let $L = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\{L_t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\}_{t \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathcal T^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{pauli}}}$ be the family of Definition~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{def:pauli-question-distribution}. Then the question distribution of $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathfrak{G}^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{Pauli}}_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathsf{qldparams}}$ is the $(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathcal T^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{pauli}}, G^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{pauli}})$-typed conditionally linear distribution $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mu^{G^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{pauli}}}_{L,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\,L}$ of Definition~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{def:typed-cl-distributions}. As in Lemma~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{lem:ld-question-typed-cl}, the linked declaration states the distribution identity alone: an equality between the question sampler of $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathfrak{G}^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{Pauli}}_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathsf{qldparams}}$ and the distribution that the construction of Definition~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{def:typed-cl-distributions} produces from the pair $(L, L)$ and the graph $G^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{pauli}}$, a construction that is available for an arbitrary family of maps. Neither that equality nor the assertion that $L$ is a $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathcal T^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{pauli}}$-typed family of conditionally linear functions is formalized: the Lean proof of the equality is open, and so is the level assertion for the maps $L_t$ listed in Definition~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{def:pauli-question-distribution}. Both obligations are tracked as issue~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\#180, so the statement and the proof below carry no completion mark.\\\\\\\\nblueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:401:\\\\\\\\tThe type pair is drawn from $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mu_{G^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{pauli}}}$ by definition, and for each ordered type pair the content pair is the image of a single uniform $z \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\in V^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{pauli}}$ under the corresponding pair of CL functions, that is, a sample from $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mu_{L_{t_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm A}},\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\, L_{t_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm B}}}$. This is the argument of the source; it is not yet formalized, and the typed-family hypotheses on $L$ are open as well.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\nresults/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr184-20260905-04.jsonl-370-{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_189\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"nl -ba MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Apply.lean | sed -n '1,150p'\\\\\\\\nnl -ba MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Witnesses.lean | sed -n '250,325p'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":null,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"in_progress\\\\\\\"}}\\\\nresults/telemetry/sessions/reviewer-pr184-20260905-04.jsonl:371:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_189\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"nl -ba MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Apply.lean | sed -n '1,150p'\\\\\\\\nnl -ba MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Witnesses.lean | sed -n '250,325p'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"     1\\\\\\\\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Combining.Points\\\\\\\\n     2\\\\\\\\timport MIPStarRE.QPBT.Test.SoundnessDefs\\\\\\\\n     3\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n     4\\\\\\\\t/-!\\\\\\\\n     5\\\\\\\\t# Applying the classical low-degree test\\\\\\\\n     6\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n     7\\\\\\\\tThis module states the two application obligations at the end of the Pauli-basis\\\\\\\\n     8\\\\\\\\tcombining argument.  The combined-line measurement is recorded both with the error\\\\\\\\n     9\\\\\\\\tform asserted by the source and with the weaker estimate established by its first\\\\\\\\n    10\\\\\\\\tproof route.  The final witness consists of a projective measurement of a pair of\\\\\\\\n    11\\\\\\\\tglobal bounded individual-degree polynomials.  The proposition-valued declarations\\\\\\\\n    12\\\\\\\\tbelow are intentionally open proof obligations in this skeleton; their statement\\\\\\\\n    13\\\\\\\\tlinks do not claim proof closure.\\\\\\\\n    14\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    15\\\\\\\\t## References\\\\\\\\n    16\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    17\\\\\\\\tThe combined-line declarations formalize `lem:qld-4-13` in\\\\\\\\n    18\\\\\\\\t`blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex`, with paper source\\\\\\\\n    19\\\\\\\\t`references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1020-1034`.\\\\\\\\n    20\\\\\\\\tThe global-pair declaration formalizes `lem:qld-4-7` in the same blueprint, with\\\\\\\\n    21\\\\\\\\tpaper source\\\\\\\\n    22\\\\\\\\t`references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1267-1274`.\\\\\\\\n    23\\\\\\\\t-/\\\\\\\\n    24\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    25\\\\\\\\tnamespace MIPStarRE.QPBT\\\\\\\\n    26\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    27\\\\\\\\tnoncomputable section\\\\\\\\n    28\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    29\\\\\\\\t/-- Conditional construction of the extended-line measurements with the source error\\\\\\\\n    30\\\\\\\\t`poly(m^2 * epsilon, md / q)`.  This is the source-facing statement of\\\\\\\\n    31\\\\\\\\t`lem:qld-4-13`, paper lines 1020--1034.\\\\\\\\n    32\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    33\\\\\\\\tThe printed proof does not establish this error form: its first route gives\\\\\\\\n    34\\\\\\\\t`m * poly(epsilon, md / q)`, while its second route gives a different bound and\\\\\\\\n    35\\\\\\\\tuses a joint-law decomposition absent from the subline lemma.  The discrepancy is\\\\\\\\n    36\\\\\\\\tdocumented in `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_combined-lines-error-term.tex` and\\\\\\\\n    37\\\\\\\\t`rem:qld-4-13-source-defects` in the blueprint.  The directly indexed line carrier\\\\\\\\n    38\\\\\\\\tused by `ExtendedLinesWitness` represents the required extended-dimensional\\\\\\\\n    39\\\\\\\\tline-point law without the invalid divisibility guard; it is a directly indexed\\\\\\\\n    40\\\\\\\\tline-space construction and does\\\\\\\\n    41\\\\\\\\tnot identify the source's seed-bearing verifier game with the directly indexed game.\\\\\\\\n    42\\\\\\\\tThis declaration takes an already constructed point witness; the\\\\\\\\n    43\\\\\\\\tsource-facing declaration below supplies that witness existentially.\\\\\\\\n    44\\\\\\\\t-/\\\\\\\\n    45\\\\\\\\ttheorem exists_extendedLinesWitness_ofPointsWitness :\\\\\\\\n    46\\\\\\\\t    ∃ deltaCombine : ℝ → ℝ → ℝ, IsPolyErr₂ deltaCombine ∧\\\\\\\\n    47\\\\\\\\t      ∀ (P : AdmissibleParams) (ε δQ : ℝ) (S : ProjectiveSetting P ε)\\\\\\\\n    48\\\\\\\\t        (points : CombinedPointsWitness S δQ),\\\\\\\\n    49\\\\\\\\t        Nonempty (ExtendedLinesWitness S points\\\\\\\\n    50\\\\\\\\t          (deltaCombine ((P.m : ℝ) ^ 2 * ε)\\\\\\\\n    51\\\\\\\\t            ((P.m * P.d : ℕ) / (P.q : ℝ)))) := by\\\\\\\\n    52\\\\\\\\t  sorry\\\\\\\\n    53\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    54\\\\\\\\t/-! The source-facing declaration supplies the point witness from\\\\\\\\n    55\\\\\\\\t`lem:qld-4-10` rather than taking it as an unproved external hypothesis. -/\\\\\\\\n    56\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    57\\\\\\\\t/-- The source-facing extended-line construction of `lem:qld-4-13`, paper\\\\\\\\n    58\\\\\\\\tlines 1020--1034.\\\\\\\\n    59\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    60\\\\\\\\tThe `_ofPointsWitness` companion is the conditional, Lean-only form retained\\\\\\\\n    61\\\\\\\\tfor calculations that already have a point witness. -/\\\\\\\\n    62\\\\\\\\ttheorem exists_extendedLinesWitness :\\\\\\\\n    63\\\\\\\\t    ∃ deltaQ : ℝ → ℝ, IsPolyErr deltaQ ∧\\\\\\\\n    64\\\\\\\\t      ∃ deltaCombine : ℝ → ℝ → ℝ, IsPolyErr₂ deltaCombine ∧\\\\\\\\n    65\\\\\\\\t        ∀ (P : AdmissibleParams) (ε : ℝ) (S : ProjectiveSetting P ε),\\\\\\\\n    66\\\\\\\\t          ∃ points : CombinedPointsWitness S (deltaQ ε),\\\\\\\\n    67\\\\\\\\t            Nonempty (ExtendedLinesWitness S points\\\\\\\\n    68\\\\\\\\t              (deltaCombine ((P.m : ℝ) ^ 2 * ε)\\\\\\\\n    69\\\\\\\\t                ((P.m * P.d : ℕ) / (P.q : ℝ)))) := by\\\\\\\\n    70\\\\\\\\t  sorry\\\\\\\\n    71\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    72\\\\\\\\t/-- Construction of the extended-line measurements with the estimate actually\\\\\\\\n    73\\\\\\\\tdelivered by the first proof route, `C * m * poly(epsilon, md / q)`.\\\\\\\\n    74\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    75\\\\\\\\tThis is an established auxiliary form of the argument, not the source-labelled\\\\\\\\n    76\\\\\\\\t`lem:qld-4-13`; it must not be advertised as that theorem.  The source discrepancy\\\\\\\\n    77\\\\\\\\tis analyzed in `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_combined-lines-error-term.tex`.  As in the\\\\\\\\n    78\\\\\\\\tsource-facing declaration, the extended questions use the directly indexed line-space\\\\\\\\n    79\\\\\\\\tconstruction.  This conditional declaration takes an already constructed point witness;\\\\\\\\n    80\\\\\\\\tthe source-facing construction below supplies it existentially.  Relating its game to the source's\\\\\\\\n    81\\\\\\\\tseed-bearing game requires the transport\\\\\\\\n    82\\\\\\\\tand soundness obligations in\\\\\\\\n    83\\\\\\\\t`docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex`.\\\\\\\\n    84\\\\\\\\t-/\\\\\\\\n    85\\\\\\\\ttheorem exists_extendedLinesWitness_established_ofPointsWitness :\\\\\\\\n    86\\\\\\\\t    ∃ C : ℝ, 0 < C ∧\\\\\\\\n    87\\\\\\\\t      ∃ deltaCombine : ℝ → ℝ → ℝ, IsPolyErr₂ deltaCombine ∧\\\\\\\\n    88\\\\\\\\t        ∀ (P : AdmissibleParams) (ε δQ : ℝ) (S : ProjectiveSetting P ε)\\\\\\\\n    89\\\\\\\\t          (points : CombinedPointsWitness S δQ),\\\\\\\\n    90\\\\\\\\t          Nonempty (ExtendedLinesWitness S points\\\\\\\\n    91\\\\\\\\t            (C * (P.m : ℝ) *\\\\\\\\n    92\\\\\\\\t              deltaCombine ε ((P.m * P.d : ℕ) / (P.q : ℝ)))) := by\\\\\\\\n    93\\\\\\\\t  sorry\\\\\\\\n    94\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    95\\\\\\\\t/-- Source-facing construction for the established auxiliary estimate.  This is\\\\\\\\n    96\\\\\\\\tthe same Lean-only bound as `exists_extendedLinesWitness_established_ofPointsWitness`,\\\\\\\\n    97\\\\\\\\twith the point witness existentially supplied rather than assumed. -/\\\\\\\\n    98\\\\\\\\ttheorem exists_extendedLinesWitness_established :\\\\\\\\n    99\\\\\\\\t    ∃ deltaQ : ℝ → ℝ, IsPolyErr deltaQ ∧\\\\\\\\n   100\\\\\\\\t      ∃ C : ℝ, 0 < C ∧\\\\\\\\n   101\\\\\\\\t        ∃ deltaCombine : ℝ → ℝ → ℝ, IsPolyErr₂ deltaCombine ∧\\\\\\\\n   102\\\\\\\\t          ∀ (P : AdmissibleParams) (ε : ℝ) (S : ProjectiveSetting P ε),\\\\\\\\n   103\\\\\\\\t            ∃ points : CombinedPointsWitness S (deltaQ ε),\\\\\\\\n   104\\\\\\\\t              Nonempty (ExtendedLinesWitness S points\\\\\\\\n   105\\\\\\\\t                (C * (P.m : ℝ) *\\\\\\\\n   106\\\\\\\\t                  deltaCombine ε ((P.m * P.d : ℕ) / (P.q : ℝ)))) := by\\\\\\\\n   107\\\\\\\\t  sorry\\\\\\\\n   108\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   109\\\\\\\\t/-- Construction of the projective global polynomial-pair measurements from\\\\\\\\n   110\\\\\\\\t`lem:qld-4-7`, paper lines 1267--1274.  The statement has the source's universal\\\\\\\\n   111\\\\\\\\tconstants and contains no divisibility hypothesis or residual construction input.\\\\\\\\n   112\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   113\\\\\\\\tThe argument uses low-degree soundness at dimension `2 * m + 2`.  The current\\\\\\\\n   114\\\\\\\\tdirect carrier realizes the required dimension without assuming\\\\\\\\n   115\\\\\\\\t`2 * m + 2 ∣ q`, but it does not itself prove the game-correspondence and\\\\\\\\n   116\\\\\\\\tauxiliary-parameter estimates required by the soundness import; those obligations\\\\\\\\n   117\\\\\\\\tare exposed by `exists_direct_ld_soundness` and documented in\\\\\\\\n   118\\\\\\\\t`docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex`.  Absorption of the established\\\\\\\\n   119\\\\\\\\tcombined-lines prefactor into the final universal constants is to use\\\\\\\\n   120\\\\\\\\t`deltaQld_mono` on its stated source parameter domain.\\\\\\\\n   121\\\\\\\\t-/\\\\\\\\n   122\\\\\\\\ttheorem exists_globalPairWitness :\\\\\\\\n   123\\\\\\\\t    ∃ a b : ℝ, 1 < a ∧ 0 < b ∧ b < 1 ∧\\\\\\\\n   124\\\\\\\\t      ∀ (P : AdmissibleParams) (ε : ℝ), 0 < ε →\\\\\\\\n   125\\\\\\\\t        ∀ S : ProjectiveSetting P ε,\\\\\\\\n   126\\\\\\\\t          Nonempty (GlobalPairWitness S (deltaQld a b ε P.m P.d P.q)) := by\\\\\\\\n   127\\\\\\\\t  sorry\\\\\\\\n   128\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   129\\\\\\\\tend\\\\\\\\n   130\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   131\\\\\\\\tend MIPStarRE.QPBT\\\\\\\\n   250\\\\\\\\t  /-- Each line triple carries affine data sufficient for\\\\\\\\n   251\\\\\\\\t  `combineLinePoly_spec`. -/\\\\\\\\n   252\\\\\\\\t  compatibility : ∀ sample ∈ D.support,\\\\\\\\n   253\\\\\\\\t    ∃ aX bX aZ bZ uAlpha vAlpha uBeta vBeta : PauliScalar P,\\\\\\\\n   254\\\\\\\\t      IsCombineLineCompatible\\\\\\\\n   255\\\\\\\\t        (directPointToPauli P sample.1.base)\\\\\\\\n   256\\\\\\\\t        (directPointToPauli P sample.1.direction)\\\\\\\\n   257\\\\\\\\t        sample.2.1.base sample.2.1.direction\\\\\\\\n   258\\\\\\\\t        sample.2.2.base sample.2.2.direction\\\\\\\\n   259\\\\\\\\t        aX bX aZ bZ uAlpha vAlpha uBeta vBeta\\\\\\\\n   260\\\\\\\\t  /-- Each one-point projected marginal is a mixture of restricted product\\\\\\\\n   261\\\\\\\\t  laws.  No equality for their joint conditional law is claimed. -/\\\\\\\\n   262\\\\\\\\t  source_mixture : ∃ components : Distribution (SubLineComponent P),\\\\\\\\n   263\\\\\\\\t    components.IsProbability ∧\\\\\\\\n   264\\\\\\\\t      (subLinePointDist P D).map subLineXProjection =\\\\\\\\n   265\\\\\\\\t        Distribution.bind components (subLineXComponentDist P) ∧\\\\\\\\n   266\\\\\\\\t      (subLinePointDist P D).map subLineZProjection =\\\\\\\\n   267\\\\\\\\t        Distribution.bind components (subLineZComponentDist P)\\\\\\\\n   268\\\\\\\\t  /-- An extended axis line has axis-parallel projected lines. -/\\\\\\\\n   269\\\\\\\\t  axis_closure : ∀ sample ∈ D.support, sample.1.kind = .axis ->\\\\\\\\n   270\\\\\\\\t    sample.2.1.kind = .axis ∧ sample.2.2.kind = .axis\\\\\\\\n   271\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   272\\\\\\\\t/-! ## Extended lines and global polynomial pairs -/\\\\\\\\n   273\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   274\\\\\\\\t/-- Extended-line POVMs and the two source consistency displays from\\\\\\\\n   275\\\\\\\\t`lem:qld-4-13`, paper lines 1020--1034.  The direct line carrier avoids the\\\\\\\\n   276\\\\\\\\tdimension-divisibility obstruction documented in\\\\\\\\n   277\\\\\\\\t`docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex`. -/\\\\\\