\\\\\in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mH_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\alice \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\otimes \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mH_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bob$ and $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mH_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\alice''},\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mH_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bob''} \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\cong (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\C^q)^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\otimes M}$ with $M = 2^m$) and a state $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\aux} \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mH_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\alice'} \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\otimes \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mH_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bob'}$ such that \\\\\\\\n    11\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\begin{enumerate}\\\\\\\\n    12\\\\\\\\t    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\item $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\left \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\| \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\phi_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\alice \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\otimes \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\phi_B \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\psi} - \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\aux} \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\otimes \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\EPR_q}^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\otimes M}  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\right \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\| \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leq \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\qld}(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\eps,m,d,q)$,\\\\\\\\n    13\\\\\\\\t    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\item Letting $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\tilde{A}^x_a = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\phi_A\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\, A^x_a \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\phi_A^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\dagger$ and $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\tilde{B}^y_b = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\phi_B B^y_b \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\phi_B^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\dagger$, we have for $W \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\{X,Z\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\}$\\\\\\\\n    14\\\\\\\\t    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\begin{gather*}\\\\\\\\n    15\\\\\\\\t        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\tilde{A}^{(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\pauli,W)}_u \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\otimes I_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bob'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bob''} \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\approx_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\qld}} (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\tau^W_u)_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\alice''} \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\otimes I_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\alice' \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bob' \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bob''} \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    16\\\\\\\\t        I_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\alice'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\alice''} \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\otimes \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\tilde{B}^{(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\pauli,W)}_u    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\approx_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\qld}} I_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\alice' \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\alice'' \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bob'} \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\otimes (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\tau^W_u)_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bob''}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\;,\\\\\\\\n    17\\\\\\\\t    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\end{gather*}\\\\\\\\n    18\\\\\\\\t    where the $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\approx_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\qld}}$ statement holds with respect to the state $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\aux}_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\alice'\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bob'} \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\otimes \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\EPR_q}^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\otimes M}_{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\alice''\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\bob''}$ and the answer summation is over $u \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_q^M$.\\\\\\\\n    19\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\end{enumerate}\\\\\\\\n    20\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\end{theorem}\\\\\\\\n    21\\\\\\\\tWe also recall the meaning of the parameters: $q$ is the field size,\\\\\\\\n    22\\\\\\\\t$m$ the number of variables, $d$ the degree of the low-degree code,\\\\\\\\n    23\\\\\\\\tand $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nqubits=2^m$ is the number of $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\EPR_q}$ states being tested for.\\\\\\\\n    24\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    25\\\\\\\\tThis appendix is structured as follows. First, we establish some preliminary facts and definitions \\\\\\\\n    26\\\\\\\\tin \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Cref{sec:qld-prelim}. In the remainder of the appendix, we\\\\\\\\n    27\\\\\\\\tshow \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Cref{thm:pauli-appendix} by showing how to construct a representation of\\\\\\\\n    28\\\\\\\\tthe Pauli group on the provers' Hilbert space, starting from a\\\\\\\\n    29\\\\\\\\tstrategy $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\strategy$ that succeeds in $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\game^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\pauli_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\qldparams$ with\\\\\\\\n    30\\\\\\\\thigh probability. This is done in several stages: in\\\\\\\\n    31\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Cref{sec:commutation}, we use the strategy measurements to define a\\\\\\\\n    32\\\\\\\\tset of observables that correspond to a subset of the Pauli $X$ and\\\\\\\\n    33\\\\\\\\t$Z$ observables, and show that these\\\\\\\\n    34\\\\\\\\tapproximately satisfy the associated Pauli group relations. In \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Cref{sec:expanding},\\\\\\\\n    35\\\\\\\\twe adjoin ancillary registers containing EPR states to the provers'\\\\\\\\n    36\\\\\\\\tstate $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\psi}$, and define a new set of approximately-commuting\\\\\\\\n    37\\\\\\\\tobservables acting on the expanded state. In \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Cref{sec:combining}, we\\\\\\\\n    38\\\\\\\\tcombine the approximately-commuting observables into a strategy for\\\\\\\\n    39\\\\\\\\tthe \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\emph{classical} low-degree test, and in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Cref{sec:apply-ldt}, we\\\\\\\\n    40\\\\\\\\tapply the soundness theorem of the classical low-degree test to\\\\\\\\n    41\\\\\\\\tconstruct a single projective measurement that simultaneously measures all of the\\\\\\\\n    42\\\\\\\\tapproximately-commuting observables. Finally, in\\\\\\\\n    43\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Cref{sec:separating}, we use this single simultaneous measurement to\\\\\\\\n    44\\\\\\\\tconstruct an exact representation of the Pauli group, show that it\\\\\\\\n    45\\\\\\\\tis close to the original strategy observables on the expanded state, and deduce that the game $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\game^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\pauli_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\qldparams$ is a self-test for the strategy $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\strategy^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\pauli$.\\\\\\\\n    46\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    47\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\subsection{Preliminaries}\\\\\\\\n    48\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\label{sec:qld-prelim}\\\\\\\\n    49\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    50\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    51\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\begin{definition}\\\\\\\\n    52\\\\\\\\tGiven integer $d,m$ and a prime power $q$ we denote by $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ideg_{d,m}(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_q)$ the set of polynomials in $m$ variables\\\\\\\\n    53\\\\\\\\t  with \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\emph{individual} degree at most $d$ in each variable. When the field is clear from context we write $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ideg_{d,m}$. \\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    54\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\tWhen\\\\\\\\n    55\\\\\\\\t  the number of variables is clear from context we\\\\\\\\n    56\\\\\\\\t  write $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ideg_d$. We denote by $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\deg_{d}$ the set of polynomials with\\\\\\\\n    57\\\\\\\\t  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\emph{total} degree at most $d$.\\\\\\\\n    58\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\end{definition}\\\\\\\\n    59\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    60\\\\\\\\tRecall the low-degree code defined in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\Cref{sec:ld-encoding}, in which vectors $h \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_q^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nqubits$ get mapped to polynomials $g_h \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ideg_{d,m}(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_q)$ such that for every $u \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\{0,1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\}^m$, $g_h(u) = h_u$ where the coordinates of $h$ are indexed by binary strings of length $m$. For $x\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_q^m$, recall the definition of the vector $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ind_m(x) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_q^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nqubits$ from Section~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{sec:ld-encoding}. Recall also the finite field trace $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\tr(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\cdot)=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\tr_{q\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\to 2}(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\cdot):\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_q\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\to\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_2$, where $q=2^k$ for odd $k$, defined in Section~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{sec:subfields}. \\\\\\\\n    61\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    62\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    63\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    64\\\\\\\\tCall a tuple $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\omega = (u_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\xpt,u_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\zpt,r_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\xpt,r_\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\zpt) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\in (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_q^m)^2\\\\\\\\n    65\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\times (\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_q)^2$ \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\emph{anticommuting} if the quantity \\\\\\\\n    66\\\\\\\\t \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\gamma\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\,=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\