\\\\\mathcal{G}$ denote the set of such polynomials. On average over uniformly random $(x,z,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\alpha,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\beta)$, \\\\\\\\n     1\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\chapter{Strategy observables and the expanded space}\\\\\\\\n     2\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\label{chap:qpbt-observables}\\\\\\\\n     3\\\\\\\\t% This chapter covers the first three subsections of the source appendix\\\\\\\\n     4\\\\\\\\t% ``Analysis of the Pauli basis test''\\\\\\\\n     5\\\\\\\\t% (references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex, lines 1-679).\\\\\\\\n     6\\\\\\\\t% The paper's subsection labels sec:qld-prelim, sec:commutation and\\\\\\\\n     7\\\\\\\\t% sec:expanding are kept on the sections below for cross-reference fidelity.\\\\\\\\n     8\\\\\\\\t% The source restates thm:pauli verbatim at the head of the appendix under the\\\\\\\\n     9\\\\\\\\t% label thm:pauli-appendix (lines 6-20); the statement is the same theorem, and\\\\\\\\n    10\\\\\\\\t% all references here are to thm:pauli as stated in Chapter chap:qpbt-test.\\\\\\\\n    11\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    12\\\\\\\\tThis chapter and the two that follow contain the proof of the soundness\\\\\\\\n    13\\\\\\\\ttheorem for the Pauli basis test, Theorem~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{thm:pauli}, stated in\\\\\\\\n    14\\\\\\\\tChapter~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{chap:qpbt-test}. Starting from a strategy that succeeds in the\\\\\\\\n    15\\\\\\\\tgame $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathfrak{G}^{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathrm{Pauli}}_{(q,m,d)}$ with high probability, the proof\\\\\\\\n    16\\\\\\\\tconstructs a representation of the Pauli group on the players' Hilbert space\\\\\\\\n    17\\\\\\\\tin several stages. In Section~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{sec:commutation} the strategy measurements\\\\\\\\n    18\\\\\\\\tare used to define a set of observables that correspond to a subset of the\\\\\\\\n    19\\\\\\\\tPauli $X$ and $Z$ observables, and these observables are shown to\\\\\\\\n    20\\\\\\\\tapproximately satisfy the associated Pauli group relations. In\\\\\\\\n    21\\\\\\\\tSection~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{sec:expanding}, ancillary registers containing EPR states are\\\\\\\\n    22\\\\\\\\tadjoined to the players' state, and a new set of approximately commuting\\\\\\\\n    23\\\\\\\\tobservables acting on the expanded state is defined.\\\\\\\\n    24\\\\\\\\tChapter~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{chap:qpbt-combining} combines the approximately commuting\\\\\\\\n    25\\\\\\\\tobservables into a strategy for the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\emph{classical} low individual degree\\\\\\\\n    26\\\\\\\\ttest and applies the soundness theorem of that test to construct a single\\\\\\\\n    27\\\\\\\\tprojective measurement that simultaneously measures all of them.\\\\\\\\n    28\\\\\\\\tChapter~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{chap:qpbt-extraction} uses this simultaneous measurement to\\\\\\\\n    29\\\\\\\\tconstruct an exact representation of the Pauli group, shows that it is close\\\\\\\\n    30\\\\\\\\tto the original strategy observables on the expanded state, and deduces\\\\\\\\n    31\\\\\\\\tTheorem~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{thm:pauli}. Section~\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ref{sec:qld-prelim} below collects\\\\\\\\n    32\\\\\\\\tpreliminary definitions and lemmas used throughout the analysis.\\\\\\\\n    33\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n    34\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\section{Preliminaries}\\\\\\\\n    35\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\label{sec:qld-prelim}\\\\\\\\n   360\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\tpointwise inequality.\\\\\\\\n   361\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\end{proof}\\\\\\\\n   362\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\n   363\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\begin{lemma}\\\\\\\\n   364\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\label{lem:povm-to-obs}\\\\\\\\n   365\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\lean{MIPStarRE.QPBT.povm_to_obs_of_measurements}\\\\\\\\n   366\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\leanok\\\\\\\\n   367\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\uses{def:approx-question-indexed-operators, def:povm-distance}\\\\\\\\n   368\\\\\\\\t\\\\\\\\tLet $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\mathcal{A}$ be a finite set, let $\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\{A^x_a\\\\\