  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-review pr=400 head=37a2e268bc1ef7434e13c9b8b3daf3c02d18b94e -->\n# Review \u2014 PR 400 @ 37a2e268bc1e\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED (code=CHANGES_REQUESTED, prose=CHANGES_REQUESTED)\n\nPosted by `local/bin/review.sh` at 2026-09-08T21:35:27Z \u2014 the local replacement for the `code-review` and `prose-review` jobs of `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`.\n\nBranch `issue-387-recover-subline-z-term` onto `main`; merge base `628e3b533ceed0d061c96d610465852bc4ad4610`; head `37a2e268bc1ef7434e13c9b8b3daf3c02d18b94e`.\n\n## Findings\n\nCheckbox states: `[ ]` unresolved (blocks the merge), `[x]` resolved.\nResolve a finding by ticking its box in this review body.\n\n<!-- findings:begin -->\n- [ ] F1 (blocker) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Claims.lean:340` \u2014 Keep the directly indexed Claim 17-1/17-3 results distinct from the source theorems until the carrier and distribution transport is established.  <!-- lane=code -->\n- [ ] F2 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Claims.lean:240` \u2014 Replace duplicated completion and uniform-line proofs with the support lemmas supplied by this same PR.  <!-- lane=code -->\n- [ ] F3 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1564` \u2014 Claim 17-1 certifies a complex scalar bound, but Lean bounds only real parts.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F4 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1588` \u2014 The newly certified proof retains an incorrect squared operator and mismatched constants.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F5 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/SubLinePrefix.lean:11` \u2014 The description reverses which coordinate blocks vanish under prefix truncation.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F6 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/SubLineUniform.lean:57` \u2014 The fiber argument incorrectly says the canonical representative varies over a coset.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F7 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/ZEvalDeficit.lean:13` \u2014 The module documentation claims X-point estimates absent from this change.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n<!-- findings:end -->\n\n## Code review\n\nF1: Claims 17-1 and 17-3 use the distribution from the source subline lemma (`references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1063-1067`, `1140-1145`, `1204-1209`). The Lean results quantify over `SubLineWitness`, whose extended marginal is `directLinePointDist`. `Witnesses.lean:245` explicitly identifies this as an auxiliary record, while `Lines.lean:245` says transport to the source carrier remains open. Nevertheless, Claim 17-1 is newly marked `\\leanok` at `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1564`, and both theorem docstrings identify their results directly with the source claims. The proofs establish useful results on the direct carrier; they do not discharge that documented source-domain discrepancy. State their direct scope explicitly and leave the source-labelled completion pending, or supply the missing transport. This must be fixed before merge.\n\nF2: `completed_pair_norm_sq_sum` duplicates the already imported `ProjectiveSetting.completedPair_norm_sq_sum_ZX` from `ZEvalDeficit.lean:165`. Its entire proof can be replaced by `exact S.completedPair_norm_sq_sum_ZX points .BA'' x z`. Likewise, `UniformLinePoint.lean:80` copies the fiber-counting proof of `Lines/SubLineUniform.lean:61`. Both proposed applications passed focused Lean checks. Reuse those declarations to avoid maintaining and elaborating parallel implementations of the same identities.\n\nThe full 27-file diff was inspected, and its hash matches the canonical patch. The clean local and remote heads agree; all nine exact-head CI contexts were green. Fresh elaboration of the current Claims source passed, with only the retained Claim 17-2 `sorry`. Axiom inspection of Claims 17-1/17-3, `exists_subLineWitness`, and `restricted_lines_consistency_bound` found only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n\nThe universal constants remain outside all parameter quantifiers. The implemented Claims 17-1/17-3 bounds use `C = 2`; the Z proof uses the separate Z marginal and derives its deficit without Claim 17-2. No new proof holes, bypasses, or load-bearing hypotheses were found. Claim 17-2\u2019s existing arbitrary-witness contract remains unresolved on this head; the separate repairs are not current proof content. The prose lane owns the distinct complex-scalar versus real-part comparison.\n\nThe external `lean-conventions` skill was unavailable; checked-in conventions were used. No files or workflow records were modified.\n\nNative review binding: 48c8adbc83d749b0b79fb9faac681534 37a2e268bc1ef7434e13c9b8b3daf3c02d18b94e 513a56fa3336424731bec2e678fa15c8bbf06f6bb83e4c4542edb1fba2c18b9e\n\n## Prose review\n\nF1: The blueprint defines scalar approximation by the absolute difference at lines 46\u201347 and displays the expectations themselves in Claim 17-1. However, `Claims.lean:360` and `Claims.lean:375` take real parts before averaging. The ordered product of the two point projections need not be Hermitian, and no reality assertion accompanies this signature. A bound on the real part does not establish the displayed complex modulus bound. Prove the complex overlap estimate, or record the real-part result separately without certifying the paper statement.\n\nF2: The proof at blueprint lines 1604\u20131609 uses \\(W^2\\), bounds its expectation by \\(\\delta_Q\\), and concludes an error at most \\(\\sqrt{\\delta_Q}\\). For \\(W=Q-M_ZM_X\\), the squared norm involves \\(W^\\dagger W\\). Moreover, `OrderedPoints.lean:46` supplies \\(4\\delta_Q\\), and `Claims.lean:377` chooses the universal constant \\(2\\). Rewrite the sketch using \\(W^\\dagger W\\), \\(4\\delta_Q\\), and \\(2\\sqrt{\\delta_Q}\\); the advertised asymptotic error remains unchanged.\n\nF3: Replace \u201cthe preceding block is retained untruncated, and every later block vanishes\u201d with \u201cpreceding blocks vanish, and later blocks remain untruncated.\u201d For examp