  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-review pr=400 head=b94bd06f0c2b69579f97c065c44fe63f71f8c0d6 -->\n# Review \u2014 PR 400 @ b94bd06f0c2b\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED (code=APPROVED, prose=CHANGES_REQUESTED)\n\nPosted by `local/bin/review.sh` at 2026-09-09T05:29:42Z \u2014 the local replacement for the `code-review` and `prose-review` jobs of `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`.\n\nBranch `issue-387-recover-subline-z-term` onto `main`; merge base `a111c34ab3ca8b0db115b73156ddcd5bf886e9f8`; head `b94bd06f0c2b69579f97c065c44fe63f71f8c0d6`.\n\n## Findings\n\nCheckbox states: `[ ]` unresolved (blocks the merge), `[x]` resolved.\nResolve a finding by ticking its box in this review body.\n\n<!-- findings:begin -->\n- [ ] F1 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1245` \u2014 The new certification includes a field-valued consistency statement, but Lean proves a completed coefficient-answer bound.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F2 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1225` \u2014 The certified restricted-axis definition omits the seed-bearing refinement retained by its Lean counterpart.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n<!-- findings:end -->\n\n## Code review\n\nReviewed head `b94bd06f0c2b69579f97c065c44fe63f71f8c0d6` using the on-disk patch and full prior ledger.\n\nPrior findings are addressed:\n- Code F1 and prose F3: Claims 17-1/17-3 now have separate auxiliary blueprint entries explicitly stating the direct-indexed law and real-part conclusions. The source claims remain pending.\n- Code F2: the flagged completion and uniform-line proof bodies reuse the shared lemmas.\n- Prose F4: the calculation uses `W\u2020W`, squared-distance bound `4\u03b4Q`, and overlap bound `2\u221a\u03b4Q`.\n- Prose F5/F6/F7 and the later prose F1: the identified descriptions and auxiliary mathematical notation are corrected.\n\nStatement integrity: the restricted-distribution estimates preserve the paper\u2019s `2m` and `4m\u00b2` factors (`references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1049`). The scalar results retain universal constants outside parameter quantifiers and introduce no new proof-obligation inputs. Their differences from `claim:17-1` and `claim:17-3` are explicitly documented, not advertised as completed source formalizations.\n\nVerification: `Claims.lean` and `Lines.lean` type-check with only their three unchanged, documented proof-hole warnings. Axiom checks for both completed scalar claims, subline existence, restricted consistency, and the mixture identity contain no `sorryAx`. `git diff --check` passes; the checkout remains unchanged.\n\nResidual work remains on Claim 17-2, the existing measurement constructions, source-distribution transport, and the complex overlap statement. Full build and blueprint rendering were not rerun.\n\n## Prose review\n\n**F1: Outcome-space mismatch.** Equation `eq:qld-xz-lines-restricted` at blueprint line 1274 uses polynomial functions on lines, as explicitly defined at lines 52\u201354. However, [Lines.lean](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/.worktrees/issue-387-recover-subline-z-term/MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines.lean:203) bounds consistency after evaluating coefficient-list answers into the completed alphabet.\n\nThis distinction matters on zero-direction lines: the coefficient polynomial \\(f(t)=t\\) has no well-defined value on the singleton line under `EvaluatesTo`, whereas a function on that singleton necessarily does. The witness does not require such coefficient answers to have zero effect. Consequently, the newly added statement and proof `\\leanok` markers do not certify the displayed source statement. Separate the completed-answer estimate into an explicitly auxiliary entry, preserving the source statement without certification until the correspondence is established. The source-faithful mixture and nonnegative-average results can be certified separately.\n\n**F2: Distribution-carrier mismatch.** The restricted-axis definition at blueprint lines 1227\u20131231 describes pairs with an axis line \\((u_0,e_i)\\). In contrast, [Defs.lean](/home/drx/MIPStarRE-qpbt/.worktrees/issue-387-recover-subline-z-term/MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Defs.lean:414) returns seed-bearing line descriptions, retaining the residual seed even after conditioning on its coordinate index. Different seeds selecting the same axis remain distinct outcomes. Chapter 13 already explicitly distinguishes these refined laws from their source push-forwards at line 177. Make the same distinction here, linking Lean to the refined restriction and describing the source restriction through the seed-forgetting map.\n\nPrior-feedback disposition: prose findings F3\u2013F7 and the later prose F1 are resolved. The Claim 17-1/17-3 source-scope concern is addressed by the separate auxiliary entries. The code-only duplication finding remains for the code reviewer to adjudicate.\n\nSummary: **2 equivalence/status findings; no additional prose-language findings.** The truncated attachment was supplemented with the on-disk patch and checkout. This was a static, read-only review; builds and rendering were not rerun. Source-distribution transport and the complex-overlap estimate remain explicitly open.\n",
