  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-review pr=400 head=0ddc67e8923f8d2c27cbb2fbce6ea9d495861257 -->\n# Review \u2014 PR 400 @ 0ddc67e8923f\n\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED (code=CHANGES_REQUESTED, prose=CHANGES_REQUESTED)\n\nPosted by `local/bin/review.sh` at 2026-09-09T08:33:22Z \u2014 the local replacement for the `code-review` and `prose-review` jobs of `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`.\n\nBranch `issue-387-recover-subline-z-term` onto `main`; merge base `a111c34ab3ca8b0db115b73156ddcd5bf886e9f8`; head `0ddc67e8923f8d2c27cbb2fbce6ea9d495861257`.\n\n## Findings\n\nCheckbox states: `[ ]` unresolved (blocks the merge), `[x]` resolved.\nResolve a finding by ticking its box in this review body.\n\n<!-- findings:begin -->\n- [ ] F1 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Claims.lean:44` \u2014 Reuse the shared placement, product-average, completed-effect, and line-answer regrouping APIs instead of maintaining parallel private implementations.  <!-- lane=code -->\n- [ ] F2 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/UniformLinePoint.lean:36` \u2014 Remove the duplicate bind and uniform-projection proofs and the no-op `_current` alias in favor of this PR\u2019s shared support lemmas.  <!-- lane=code -->\n- [ ] F3 (changes) `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex:440` \u2014 Identify `SubLineWitness.source_mixture` as using refined seed-bearing restrictions, not the paper\u2019s source restricted line-point laws.  <!-- lane=code -->\n- [ ] F4 (changes) `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility.tex:460` \u2014 State accurately that the joint point witness is projective while the paired-line witness is only complete.  <!-- lane=code -->\n- [ ] F5 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1247` \u2014 Certified auxiliary statements use one-based `\u03c7` indices, while Lean uses zero-based `chiIndex : Fin m`.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F6 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1257` \u2014 The definition-level `\\leanok` also certifies event-mass and source push-forward assertions absent from the linked Lean declarations.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F7 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1631` \u2014 One certified blueprint statement links independent Lean declarations with mathematically different statements.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F8 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1912` \u2014 The auxiliary claims place proof dependencies in statement `\\uses`, and the Z claim cites the unformalized source restriction lemma.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F9 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines.lean:18` \u2014 Lean documentation still advertises seed-bearing and completed-answer auxiliaries as source statements after the blueprint split.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F10 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/SubLineConstruct.lean:28` \u2014 New docstrings store stale numeric blueprint ranges instead of durable labels.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F11 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Claims.lean:21` \u2014 The module documentation contains Lean-status and software-API language.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F12 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1259` \u2014 \u201cThe formalized definitions here\u201d is a formalization progress report rather than mathematical prose.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F13 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/SubLineConstruct.lean:53` \u2014 The public `SubLineRaw` naming family uses the prohibited process-shaped term `raw`.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F14 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/UniformLinePoint.lean:78` \u2014 The public `_current` declaration is a process-named empty pass-through alias.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F15 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/RestrictedMixture.lean:142` \u2014 \u201cPublic copy\u201d, \u201cprivate\u201d, \u201cpacket\u201d, and issue-tracked duplication describe implementation history.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n- [ ] F16 (changes) `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Combining/Lines/SubLineMixture.lean:18` \u2014 \u201cThe assembly\u201d uses banned software-process terminology.  <!-- lane=prose -->\n<!-- findings:end -->\n\n## Code review\n\nF1: `Claims.lean` duplicates `ProjectiveSetting.placedMeasurement`, `avgOver_prod`, the two `pointMeasExpOption_effect_*` lemmas, and essentially all of `regroup_line_answer_sum`. The existing declarations are in `Points/PlacementSupport.lean:258-313`, `Lines/RestrictedAverage.lean:89`, and `SubLineZDeficit.lean:46-130`; the last module is already imported. These parallel implementations create two APIs for the same tensor-placement and fiber-regrouping facts and must be consolidated.\n\nF2: `Distribution.bind_const_current` duplicates `Distribution.bind_const` from `Lines/SubLineBind.lean:81`. The public `_current` theorem merely aliases `uniformDistribution_map_lineRepMap_add_smul`, while `uniformDistribution_map_projX_projZ_pauli_current` re-proves `Lines/SubLineTransport.lean:106` modulo the existing uniform-product identity. The import graph permits using those support modules without a cycle.\n\nF3: The formal components use `restrictedALineDist` and `restrictedDLineDist`, the refined seed-bearing restrictions. Blueprint `def:ith-restricted-line-refined`, lines 1236-1260, explicitly distinguishes these from their source push-forwards and notes that the axis map forgets the residual seed. Calling them \u201crestricted source line-point laws\u201d incorrectly suggests that this unresolved transport has occurred.\n\nF4: `CombinedPointsWitness.projective` establishes projectivity of `Q`, but `CombinedLinesWitness.T` at `Witnesses.lean:142-148` is only a complete `Measurement`. The blueprint correctly states \u201cprojective joint point measurements\u201d and \u201ccomplete paired-line measurements\u201d at lines 1869-1874. The paper-gap note must use the same precise hypotheses.\n\nThe earlier source-fidelity blockers are addressed: the directly indexed real-part estimates now have separate auxiliary blueprint nodes, while source Claims 17-1 and 17-3 remain uncertified pending carrier transport and the complex estimate. The restricted seed-bearing laws are also separated from the source definitions.\n\nThe supplied exact-head CI is green. `git diff --check` passes, and the only changed-file `sorry` occurrences are the clearly documented existing obligations in `Claims.lean:522` and `Lines.lean:61,90`.\n\n## Prose review\n\nCategory A is blocking.\n\n**F1.** Lean defines `chiIndex P s` as the paper\u2019s `\u03c7(s) - 1` at `Test/LowDegreeGame.lean:110`, and `restrictedLineSeedEvent` tests `chiIndex L ... = i` for `i : Fin L.m` at `Defs.lean:330`. The linked blueprint blocks instead use `\u03c7(s)=i`, sums from `1` to `m`, and `i,j\u2208{1,...,m}`. Introduce `\u03c7\u2080(s)=\u03c7(s)-1` and use indices `0,...,m-1`, or explicitly state the shift throughout lines 1246\u20131284 and 1369\u20131390. Until then, their statement-level `\\leanok` markers are invalid.\n\n**F2.** The linked declarations at `Defs.lean:414\u2013441` define the normalized restrictions and prove total mass one. They do not state that the conditioning event has probability `1/m`, nor do they formalize either displayed push-forward to the source restrictions. The event-mass theorem exists separately at `RestrictedMixture.lean:184` but is not linked; the source push-forward remains absent. Move these facts to separate theorem or remark blocks with accurate status, or restrict this certified definition to the content represented by its links.\n\n**F3.** `Placement.exists_isOpposite` at `OrderedPoints.lean:33` states an existential and symmetry property, whereas the blueprint node states only the `4\u03b4_Q` distance bound represented by `orderedZX_dist_le`. Give the existential its own support node or remove it from this node\u2019s `\\lean` list. The same issue occurs with the generic `uniformDistribution_map_uncurry` link at blueprint line 1662.\n\n**F4.** The dependencies at lines 1893 and 1912 are proof dependencies and belong in the corresponding proof blocks. In addition, the Z proof uses the seed-bearing restricted laws through `avgOver_prod_restrictedLinePointDist_le` at `ZEvalDeficit.lean:571`; it does not establish or invoke the source-law node `lem:restricted-line-mixture-bounds`. Replace that edge with `lem:restricted-line-refined-mixture-bounds`.\n\n**F5.** The blueprint now distinguishes the source nodes from `def:ith-restricted-line-refined`, `lem:restricted-line-refined-mixture-bounds`, and `lem:restricted-lines-completed-consistency`. Update the corresponding module and declaration docstrings in `Defs.lean`, `Lines.lean`, `RestrictedAverage.lean`, `RestrictedMixture.lean`, and `SubLineMixture.lean`. In particular, change `**Source statement:**` to `**Formalization-only auxiliary:**` where the seed-bearing carrier or completed coefficient answers remain present.\n\n**F6.** Remove derived blueprint line numbers from the new Lean docstrings and retain labels only. Current examples include `1209--1228` for `def:ith-restricted-line`, `445--480` for `def:combine-map`, and the obsolete chapter-14 spans in `Points/PlacementSupport.lean:17\u201321`.\n\n**F7.** Replace \u201cwithout completed Lean links\u201d with \u201cthe corresponding source claims remain open\u201d, and \u201ccurrent tensor bipartition API\u201d with \u201ccorresponding tensor bipartition\u201d. Drop the elaboration comment at `Claims.lean:268`.\n\n**F8.** Replace the sentence with mathematical scope, for example: \u201cThus `\\widetilde D_{\\mathrm v,i}` denotes the seed-bearing restriction; its source push-forward is a distinct law.\u201d\n\n**F9.** Rename the family using its mathematical role, for example `SubLineRandomness`, `subLineRandomnessDist`, `exists_randomness_of_mem_subLineDist_support`, and `subLineBranchRandomness_map_*`.\n\n**F10.** Delete `uniformDistribution_map_lineRepMap_add_smul_current` and invoke `uniformDistribution_map_lineRepMap_add_smul` directly. `_current` records implementation history and the declaration adds no mathematical content.\n\n**F11.** Drop the software-history sentence. The docstring can simply state uniformity of the retained scalar seed and cite the auxiliary blueprint construction.\n\n**F12.** Replace \u201cThe assembly is the last step\u201d with \u201cThis distributional identity is the final step\u201d.\n\nThe remaining source `\\notready` markers are justified, and the expected open source obligations are not certified by the new proof-level `\\leanok` markers. Counts: 6 category-A synchronization/status issues and 6 category-B prose/naming issues.\n",
